rovenance, liveness, range containment and access permission. Does not imply alignment or initialized/valid contents. Zero-byte write access is vacuous."},"readable_size":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Maximum nonnegative contiguous byte extent valid for reads from start in the current state, within one live provenance-compatible allocation. Zero if no positive extent is accessible. An n-byte read needs n <= readable_size for nonnegative n."},"writable_size":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Maximum nonnegative contiguous byte extent valid for writes from start under the same range/provenance rules. An n-byte write needs n <= writable_size for nonnegative n."},"initialized":{"type":"bool","meaning":"Every byte of this size-byte view has been written/initialized, including padding. Does not imply a valid typed bit pattern, alignment, liveness or permission."},"valid":{"type":"bool","meaning":"The view represents a language-valid initialized value of its associated Rust type, including discriminants/niches and required initialized bytes. Allows uninitialized padding. This is the predicate for 'properly initialized value of T'; do NOT additionally require initialized. Does not imply library safety invariants, alignment, access permission or liveness."},"allocation":{"type":"allocation","meaning":"Originating allocation record. Never inferred merely by finding a currently live allocation at the same numeric address."}},"allocation_fields":{"exists":{"type":"bool","meaning":"Whether this pointer/place has an originating allocation record."},"id":{"type":"string","meaning":"Stable allocation-generation identity. Identity/bounds fields require an existing record; same-allocation formulas must establish existence before comparing IDs. Equal originating IDs alone do not imply pointer addresses lie within the allocation: an out-of-bounds derived pointer retains its originating ID."},"start":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Allocation beginning in bytes."},"size":{"type":"integer","meani